capture_fixes = No new capture-tooling bugs were found or fixed this round; the two fixes documented for the 2.1.201->2.1.204 refresh (trace-claude-messages.cjs forwarding `input`/`init` unchanged to preserve the binary's custom `tls: { ca }` fetch option, and README.md's `--preload=./claude-code/...` `./`-prefixed path) both continued to work unmodified against 2.1.206. One new gap surfaced instead: `claude-code/misc/scripts/extract-claude-trace.cjs` only ever emits `<model>-interactive.md` prompt filenames and hardcodes `capture_modes: ["interactive"]` when merging tool variants — it has no non-interactive counterpart, so this round's non-interactive refresh (prompts/<model>.md with no suffix, and tools/*.json entries tagged `capture_modes: ["non-interactive"]`) was done with an ad hoc adaptation of that script's logic (same harness-variable redaction, same schema-based variant de-duplication) rather than a checked-in tool; a real `extract-claude-trace.cjs --mode non-interactive` (or equivalent) would remove this manual step in future rounds.
tool_notes = 2.1.204 -> 2.1.206: no prompt content changed for any of the 6 non-interactive prompt_models or the interactive claude-sonnet-5 capture beyond the embedded x-anthropic-billing-header cc_version string (2.1.204.9a9/.111 -> 2.1.206.930 for non-interactive `sdk-cli` requests, 2.1.206.d94 for the interactive `cli` request) — every prompt file's body text is byte-identical to the prior round. No eager tool schema content changed either: Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, ScheduleWakeup, Skill, and Write all matched their existing 2.1.204 variant signatures exactly (same variant groupings, same schema text; only `trace_files` provenance lists grew), and ReportFindings/ToolSearch (which have no variants — one schema shared by every model/mode) also matched byte-for-byte. AskUserQuestion was not part of this round's captures (still excluded from the non-interactive eager set, as before) and is unchanged. One genuinely new tool was observed: Artifact, seen only in this round's interactive REPL capture (claude-sonnet-5) and not present in the last-committed interactive capture (2.1.201) or anywhere in the non-interactive captures (headless `-p` mode has no web surface to publish an Artifact to) — interactive_tools grew from 10 to 11 eager tools as a result; tools/Artifact.json is new. Because the interactive capture was not re-run at 2.1.204 (only non-interactive was refreshed in that round), it is not possible to say from this repo's history alone whether Artifact first appeared in 2.1.202-2.1.206 or was already present earlier and simply never captured; flagging as new-to-this-repo rather than new-to-the-product. The non-interactive deferred-tools system-reminder list changed shape versus what 2.1.204's tool_notes documented: CronCreate, CronDelete, CronList, and LSP now DO appear in the non-interactive (-p) deferred-tools list (re-verified across 3 separate models — haiku, opus-4-7, sonnet-4-6 — all consistent), contradicting the prior claim that non-interactive request