oss repeated runs of the very same model/mode — this remains pre-existing non-deterministic harness behavior, not a 2.1.206 change, and is why misc/ still keeps only one representative non-interactive steering capture (claude-fable-5-steering.md, itself byte-identical to the 2.1.204 version) rather than one per model. Separately, the "Available agent types for the Agent tool" block inside claude-sonnet-5-interactive-steering.md changed wording for the claude-code-guide entry (now mentions Tool Runner, Managed Agents, and Claude Tag) and the block's position shifted earlier in the message — this reflects a local change to this machine's user-level `claude-code-guide` subagent definition and/or non-deterministic block ordering, not a captured Claude Code product prompt, since that list is dynamically assembled from whatever subagents are configured in the capturing environment; noted for transparency but not attributed to the 2.1.206 binary. Tool files with model-specific or capture-mode payload differences contain a variants array.
